      "summaries": {
        "en": "Supervision is an open-source Python library that provides reusable tools for computer vision tasks, eliminating repetitive boilerplate code. It offers a unified API for loading, visualizing, and filtering detections from popular models like YOLO and SAM. Key strengths include dataset annotation, model evaluation, and post-processing utilities. Use it to streamline CV pipelines, from prototyping to production, without reinventing the wheel.",
        "zh": "Supervision 是一个开源的 Python 计算机视觉工具库，旨在消除重复的样板代码，让开发者专注于核心逻辑。它提供了统一的 API，支持加载、可视化和过滤来自 YOLO、SAM 等主流模型的检测结果。核心优势包括数据集标注、模型评估和结果后处理，并内置了丰富的实用工具。你可以用它快速搭建从原型到生产的视觉流水线，无需重复造轮子。无论是目标检测、实例分割还是定向边界框任务，Supervision 都能显著提升开发效率。",
        "es": "Supervision is an open-source Python library that provides reusable tools for computer vision tasks, eliminating repetitive boilerplate code. It offers a unified API for loading, visualizing, and filtering detections from popular models like YOLO and SAM. Key strengths include dataset annotation, model evaluation, and post-processing utilities. Use it to streamline CV pipelines, from prototyping to production, without reinventing the wheel.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "supervision stands out for classification, coco, and computer-vision in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Supervision is an open-source Python library that provides reusable tools for computer vision tasks, eliminating repetitive boilerplate code. It offers a unified API for loading, visualizing, and filtering detections from popular models like YOLO and SAM. Key strengths include dataset annotation, model evaluation, and post-processing utilities. Use it to streamline CV pipelines, from prototyping to production, without reinventing the wheel.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/roboflow/supervision for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
